title: Party Disunity
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: party_disunity_timer <= 0 and (dissent >= 0.25 or wet_dissent > 40 or dry_dissent > 40 or right_dissent > 40)
on-arrival: party_disunity_timer = 4; month_actions += 1
frequency: 200

= Party Disunity

The party is quarrelling in public. Ministers brief against each other, backbenchers write to the papers, and the whips are losing count.

[? if wet_dissent > 40 : The wets think the government is wrecking the country and the party with it. ?]
[? if dry_dissent > 40 : The dries think we have lost our nerve. ?]
[? if right_dissent > 40 : The right thinks we have gone soft on immigration, crime and the Union. ?]

- @discipline: Enforce discipline.
- @wets: Make concessions to the wets.
- @dries: Reassure the dries.
- @right: Throw the right a bone.
- @easy_discard

@discipline
subtitle: -1 resource
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; dry_dissent -= 5; wet_dissent -= 5; loyalist_dissent -= 5; right_dissent -= 5; rebellion -= 1

The whips and the party chairman remind everybody that a divided party loses elections.

@wets
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 12; dry_dissent += 6; economic_liberalism -= 1; budget -= 1 if con_in_government; spending += 1 if con_in_government

A little more money for the regions and a softer tone in speeches. The wets are mollified for now.

@dries
on-arrival: dry_dissent -= 12; wet_dissent += 6; economic_liberalism += 1

A speech recommitting the government to sound money and lower taxes. The dries cheer; the wets wince.

@right
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 12; wet_dissent += 4; c1_lib += 1

Tough words on crime and immigration at the party conference. The hall is on its feet.
